## 3. Repository Structure

Target layout — additive to what exists today (packages/, scripts/, manifests/, docs/ are already real; `config/`, `hosts/`, `modules/`, `state/`, `policy/` are new):

```
dotfiles/
├── config/
│   ├── common/           # universal config: shell aliases, editor themes, .gitconfig base
│   ├── linux/             # Linux-only config
│   ├── windows/           # Windows-only config
│   └── wsl/               # WSL-specific overrides
│
├── hosts/
│   ├── linux-laptop/host.yaml
│   ├── windows-desktop/host.yaml
│   └── wsl-dev/host.yaml
│
├── modules/
│   ├── shell/ git/ terminal/ editor/ desktop/   # feature-oriented bundles, composed per profile
│
├── packages/               # existing — GNU Stow packages (bash, fish, zsh, git, vscode, cursor, etc.)
├── manifests/              # existing — dpkg.txt, flatpak.txt package lists
├── scripts/                # existing — bootstrap.sh, stow.sh, validate.sh, pull-updates.sh, push-changes.sh, install-tools.sh
├── state/                  # git-ignored — reconciler's local observed-state cache (inventory.json, drift.json, last-sync.json)
├── policy/                 # secret-scan rules, forbidden-path rules, allow-listed commit paths
├── tests/                  # idempotency tests, Stow tests, integration tests
├── docs/
│   ├── src/                # existing — the proposal/audit/synthesis chain (historical record, kept as-is)
│   └── architecture/       # ADRs — one per major decision, this file's companion
└── .github/workflows/      # consolidated CI (§9)
```

`config/` + `modules/` are **desired state**. `state/` is **observed state** and is git-ignored. `hosts/*/host.yaml` is desired state *about* a specific machine — it lives in `main`, not in a machine branch, because "this host should run profile X" is a decision, not runtime noise.

