## 6. Bootstrap Flow

Bootstrap must be safe to run any number of times, from any starting state, including mid-failure and post-reboot.

```
DISCOVER            → detect platform + environment (§4), locate or create host manifest
   ↓
VALIDATE            → check dependencies present (git, stow, shell), fail fast with a clear message
   ↓
INSTALL_DEPENDENCIES → ensure_stow(), ensure_git(), ensure_shell()  — each a no-op if already satisfied
   ↓
RESOLVE_HOST_ID     → read or create hosts/<id>/host.yaml
   ↓
ENSURE_BRANCH       → checkout machine/<hostname> if it exists; create from staging if it doesn't
   ↓
RECONCILE_SYMLINKS  → stow.sh, composed per the precedence chain in §4
   ↓
INSTALL_SERVICES    → systemd timer / Task Scheduler entry (§8), idempotent install
   ↓
VERIFY              → validate.sh; report success/failure with specifics, not just exit code
```

Each step is written as `ensure_X()` — check current state, act only if needed — never `do_X()`, which assumes a clean slate. `--dry-run` reports the plan (which steps would act) without executing any of them.

