## 8. Security Model

| Control | Mechanism | Enforced by |
|---|---|---|
| `main` cannot be pushed to directly | GitHub branch ruleset | Server (GitHub) |
| `main` requires review + passing CI | Required PR + required status check | Server (GitHub) |
| Force-push to `main` blocked | Ruleset | Server (GitHub) |
| Fast local warning against pushing to `main` | `.githooks/pre-push` | Client (advisory only) |
| Secrets never enter automated commits | Secret-pattern scan, run before any commit in §7.2 | `policy/` scan, invoked by `push-changes.sh` |
| Automated commits stay scoped | Explicit path allow-list, not `git add .` | `policy/` allow-list, invoked by `push-changes.sh` |
| Machine-generated noise never tracked | `.gitignore` + `state/` kept out of version control entirely | Git config |

**Known debt this model inherits and must clear:** `.omo/` and `.opencode/` are currently tracked despite being gitignored (added before the ignore rule). Under this architecture that's a policy violation, not just tidiness — it means the allow-list/ignore rules were bypassed once already and should be audited for what else might have slipped through the same gap.

