## 9. CI/CD Pipeline

**Current state (as of baseline commit):** `ci.yml` and `validate.yml` both trigger on push/PR to `main` and run overlapping shell/Stow validation. `comprehensive.yml` runs a scheduled matrix + Docker build. `deploy.yml` and `release.yml` handle their own concerns separately.

**Target state:**

```
PR → main
  │
  ├── static    (ShellCheck, bash -n, YAML/TOML lint)
  ├── policy    (secret scan, forbidden-path scan, allow-list check)
  ├── stow      (every package, every supported profile)
  ├── bootstrap (fresh HOME, fresh repo clone, full bootstrap run)
  └── idempotency (bootstrap run 3x, expect 0 unintended changes on runs 2–3)
        │
        ▼
      PR gate (single workflow)

Scheduled (weekly, unrelated to PR gate)
  │
  ├── Linux matrix (Ubuntu 22.04, 24.04)
  ├── WSL2 Ubuntu
  ├── Windows/PowerShell
  └── Docker build
        │
        ▼
      comprehensive.yml (unchanged responsibility, kept scoped to this)
```

`ci.yml` and `validate.yml` merge into one PR-gate workflow. `comprehensive.yml` keeps its current scheduled/matrix role untouched — the overlap being eliminated is specifically the two PR-triggered workflows duplicating each other, not the scheduled job.

